\]

ANSWER: 1.75

The covariance matrix is  

\[
\begin{bmatrix}
\text{Cov}(H,H) & \text{Cov}(H,M)\\
\text{Cov}(M,H) & \text{Cov}(M,M)
\end{bmatrix}
=
\begin{bmatrix}
256-110 & 110-81\\
110-81 & 81-0
\end{bmatrix}
=
\begin{bmatrix}
146 & 29\\
29 & 81
\end{bmatrix}.
\]

The correlation coefficient is  

\[
\rho = \frac{\text{Cov}(H,M)}{\sqrt{\text{Var}(H)\,\text{Var}(M)}}
      = \frac{29}{\sqrt{146 \times 81}}
      = \frac{29}{\sqrt{11826}}
      \approx \frac{29}{108.7}
      \approx 0.267.
\]

Thus the hedge fund’s returns are weakly positively correlated with the market index.

**ANSWER: 0.267**

The probability that a mortgage with a principal balance exceeding the collateral value is subprime is  

\[
P(\text{subprime} \mid \text{exceed}) = \frac{0.50 \times 0.50}{0.50 \times 0.50 + 0.50 \times 0.25}
= \frac{0.25}{0.25 + 0.125}
= \frac{0.25}{0.375}
= \frac{2}{3}
\approx 0.667.
\]

**ANSWER: 66.7%**

