The change in the payable salaries account is  

\[
\text{Ending payable} - \text{Beginning payable} = 1\text{M} - 3\text{M} = -2\text{M}
\]

This means the firm paid out $2 million more in salaries than it incurred.  
Since the total expense was $20 million, the cash distributed is  

\[
\text{Cash paid} = \text{Expense} + \text{Decrease in payable}
               = 20\text{M} + 2\text{M}
               = 22\text{M}
\]

**ANSWER: 22000000**

